I open the box of sweets.
I show the box.
My father asks - "Maya, what is there?"
I say - "This is a box of Indian sweets."
I show one sweet.
My father asks - "What is that?"
I say - "That is one Ladoo."
Its shape is round.
Then I show another sweet.
My mother asks - "What is that?"
I say - "That is one milk-sweet."
Its color is white.
My father says - "They are beautiful."
I say - "Yes, they are very tasty."
I ask - "Mother, what is your favorite sweet?"
Mother laughs.
I say - "But Father, you are not here."
"Mother, you are also not here."
"So I am eating all the sweets!"
